# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NSFW Firewall Engine — .gitignore
#
# Two rules govern what may be committed, and they pull in opposite directions:
#
#   1. Everything needed to BUILD, TEST, REVIEW and DEPLOY must be in Git.
#      A repository you cannot clone-and-run is documentation, not source.
#   2. Model weights and labelled evaluation corpora must NOT be in Git.
#      They are huge, licence-bound, and - in the corpus case - likely to be
#      explicit content, which §40 forbids bundling.
#
# The interesting part is that these two rules meet in the same directories
# (`models_onnx/`, `datasets/`). Those directories carry a `.gitkeep` and a
# README precisely so the *contract* is versioned while the *artifacts* are not.
# Do not "simplify" the rules below to a blanket `models_onnx/` or `datasets/`:
# that silently deletes the lockfile that `verify_models.py` checks against.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Python build & cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing comments. A `#` only opens a comment when it
# starts the line, so `*.py[cod]  # note` is matched *literally* - pattern plus
# spaces plus hash - and therefore matches nothing. Every annotation below
# therefore sits on its own line. Do not "tidy" them back onto one.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# .pyc, .pyo, .pyd
*$py.class
# Compiled extensions, in case a dependency is ever vendored.
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.whl
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Test / lint / type caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.cache/

# ── Generated protobuf / gRPC stubs ───────────────────────────────────────────
# `proto/nsfw_engine.proto` is the contract and IS committed; the generated
# `_pb2`/`_pb2_grpc` modules are build output. Regenerate with the protoc
# command in README.md ("Quick start"). They are also recompiled by the
# Dockerfile, so committing them would only create merge conflicts on every
# grpc_tools version bump.
proto/nsfw_engine_pb2.py
proto/nsfw_engine_pb2_grpc.py
proto/*_pb2.py
proto/*_pb2_grpc.py
proto/*_pb2_*.py
!proto/nsfw_engine.proto

# ── Model weights and compiled artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately scoped to file *extensions* rather than to directories, so that
# `models_onnx/README.md`, `models_onnx/.gitkeep` and `models.lock.json` keep
# being tracked. Ignoring the whole directory would drop the SHA256 lockfile
# that `scripts/verify_models.py` uses as the anti-tampering gate (§38), turning
# that gate into a no-op that always passes.
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.pth.tar
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
# torch weight dumps
*.bin
*.h5
*.tflite
*.pb
*.weights

# Locks must be committed - only the binaries are excluded. Listed explicitly as
# a guard against someone later adding a broad rule that catches them.
!models.lock.json

# ── Labelled evaluation corpora (§40, §49) ───────────────────────────────────
# `datasets/eval.example.json` — a tiny schema-only fixture — IS committed, so
# the loader and the reporting code have something to run against. Anything
# resembling a real corpus must never be: it is large, and it is very likely to
# contain the explicit material this firewall exists to filter.
#
# Ignore the data files by extension, not the directory, so the fixture and any
# accompanying schema/README survive.
datasets/**/*.jsonl
datasets/**/*.csv
datasets/**/*.parquet
datasets/**/*.tsv
datasets/**/*.npz
datasets/**/*.tar
datasets/**/*.tar.gz
datasets/**/*.zip
datasets/**/*.images
datasets/**/*.bin
# Any further real corpus, whatever its name.
datasets/*/images/
datasets/*/videos/
!datasets/eval.example.json

# ── Secrets and credentials (§18) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# `config/engine_config.yaml` is committed and must keep `api_keys: {}` empty.
# Keys are supplied at runtime via env vars / a mounted Secret; a SHA256 of a
# secret in Git is still a credential and is never committed.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets/
secrets.*
*_rsa
*_ed25519
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.kubeconfig
kubeconfig

# ── Runtime output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
*.log.*
*.pid
*.seed
*.out
*.err

# Local scratch produced by ad-hoc verification runs.
gate.txt
_smoke.py
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# ── Local databases & data volumes ───────────────────────────────────────────
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.dump
redis/
pgdata/

# ── OS / editor ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.example.json
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
nbproject/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# ── Deliberately tracked ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Listed as negations so that adding a broad rule above cannot silently drop
# these. They are the contract, not the payload.
!models_onnx/README.md
!models_onnx/.gitkeep
!datasets/eval.example.json
!config/engine_config.yaml
!config/logging_config.yaml
!config/hardware.yaml
!config/privacy.yaml
!config/quantization.yaml
!docs/
!deploy/
!tests/
!proto/nsfw_engine.proto
